    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d130">

                <pb facs="0264" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/2687</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Reinsch </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-16T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 16, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It is reported here that there is considerable dissatisfaction in China with
                    present Peking Government and that a military Government in opposition has been
                    established at Canton. It is said that thirteen provinces are supporting the
                    Peking Government and nine the Canton Government.</p>
                <p>Report by telegraph present outlook and status of situation and whether
                    opposition to Peking Government has reached proportions stated. Repeat to Canton
                    and ask for telegraphic report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
